WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:01.660
Nice to meet you.

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:02.480
We are...

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.630
IDOLiSH7!

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:09.110
<i>TRIGGER has captivated women across 
the nation in the blink of an eye.</i>

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:10.570
Until TRIGGER's concert...

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:11.900
We're not performing for a month?

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.780
Sogo-san, do you think you'd 
be able to abandon your family

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.410
for the sake of your dream?

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.410
I already have.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:22.620
It's true.

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:24.900
Why?

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:35.180
Gazing at the distant sky...

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:38.720
Someday we'll make it past there

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:44.850
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:51.150
We don't know what's right

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:54.360
So we Try and Jump!

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:57.530
Slamming face first into 
challenges and laughing

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:01.160
For us It's Only Way!

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.330
Make it shake (For Your Sky)

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.900
Make it reach (For Your Heart)

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:10.340
We'll change any and all kinds of pain

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:11.500
Do Live! (Yeah!)

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:12.340
Live! (Yeah!)

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:15.760
In the light!

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:16.840
(One, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven Go!)

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:23.020
Yes Glory Days! Together 
we'll run through them

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:25.810
If your voice (Fuu!) reverberates (Dream!)

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:29.310
Then your wishes will become 
destiny (Singing New World!)

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:35.820
Give rise now to Age of Stage!

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:42.790
The future surely lies on the other side

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:45.970
Yes... It will keep on evolving

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:49.080
Our WiSH VOYAGE

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:55.340
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:03.970
A Pro's Resolve

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:07.980
I wanna go to karaoke!

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:10.230
I wanna go to dance lessons!

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:14.450
I wanna perform concerts 
in front of our fans!

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:18.240
There're ten more days 
until the TRIGGER concert.

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:21.340
What's up, Tama?

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.940
I've had enough.

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:26.700
I'm gonna make our manager end the ban.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.370
End the ban?

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:30.510
It doesn't make sense.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:33.320
I'd understand if she told 
us <i>to</i> sing and dance.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:35.400
But <i>don't</i> dance? What the hell is that?

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.550
We're idols. There's 
something wrong with her.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.780
You don't have to put it like that.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:43.690
She thought really hard 
about what's best for us—

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:45.180
That's right.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:48.600
If you have any complaints 
for her, you can tell me.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:51.100
Why?

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:52.490
Oh, uh...

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:56.670
I'm sure she's busy.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.780
I meant to say that I'll handle them.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:01.030
<b>Slurp...</b>

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:01.030
Uh-huh...

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.290
In any case, I'm gonna go talk to her.

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:04.030
Tamaki!

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:06.820
Tamaki-kun, calm down.

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:10.370
If you talk to her when you're 
angry, you'll just scare her.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.900
What do you mean, scare her?

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.830
You're making me sound like a bad guy.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:15.770
No, it's just...

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:17.250
I think you could be more considerate—

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:19.210
Forget it, jeez!

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:20.880
Tamaki-kun!

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:24.720
I'm going to go check on him.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.480
He's like a five-year-old.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:33.770
The singing and dancing ban seems 
to be affecting Tamaki the most.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:38.690
He's so slovenly most of the time,
but full of life when he was dancing.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:42.650
Since he's not good with words, maybe 
that's how he was expressing himself.

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:44.600
I might be the same.

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:49.650
When I have trouble getting 
my point across with words,

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:52.980
I feel like singing or dancing.

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:56.710
It's like I'm releasing the 
feelings inside my body.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.120
Me, too.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.220
Me, too.

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:00.840
You might be right.

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:05.450
I wish I could sing.

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:16.210
I wanna dance.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:18.360
Tamaki-kun!

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:21.860
Tamaki-kun, let's go back.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:24.030
So-chan, you don't understand.

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:30.400
You don't complain when 
you're told to be patient.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.690
You just don't like dancing as much as I do.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:35.440
Is that how I seem to you?

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:39.210
How can you be unaffected by being 
told you can't do what you like to do?

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:41.480
It's not that I'm unaffected.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.370
I'm just used to being patient.

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:46.590
But...

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:51.290
Unless I say out loud that 
I don't like something,

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:55.250
people think I must not have
 liked it very much to begin with.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:05:01.190
If you're not patient, people
 treat you like a bad guy, though.

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:04.270
They don't hate you.

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:06.950
Relationships with other
people are hard, aren't they?

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:11.860
Let's think of the TRIGGER concert 
as a reward for our hard work.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.290
Do you know them?

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:16.580
Not really.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:18.450
I'm sure you'll like them.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.630
They're all cool, like you.

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:23.840
Really? How so?

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:25.550
Who's the best?

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:27.780
They're all amazing.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:31.200
They're talented performers 
who shot into stardom.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.470
But...

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:34.790
If I had to choose...

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:38.340
Kujo Tenn.

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:41.930
His performances are exceptional.

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:44.360
His powerful presence as the 
center is impressive, too.

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:46.280
Where did that come from?

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:48.780
The bath is free.

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:50.420
Go, before the water gets cold.

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.280
Sure, thanks.

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:55.500
Are you trying to learn from 
watching TRIGGER concerts?

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:56.910
I'm not learning from them!

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:00.790
Oh, uh... I mean, I haven't watched it yet.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:03.210
I'm gonna take a bath.

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:12.760
When you stimulate pent up emotions, they 
explode at many times the intensity.

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:18.450
I hope the stimulation you all 
provide is of the strongest variety.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:26.650
The stadium is packed!

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:28.990
The lines for merchandise are long, too!

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:30.900
We couldn't ask for better conditions!

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:34.700
If you ignore the fact that 
Tenn's in the hospital...

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:38.900
This is top secret information 
until the concert starts!

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:42.090
You boys will carry the wishes 
of your hospitalized member

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:44.010
and stand onstage with great distress,

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:44.880
are we clear?

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.340
Okay.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:49.050
Oh?

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:52.930
Hello. This is your Anesagi speaking!

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:56.120
Hospitalized for overwork, huh?

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:58.430
You think Tenn's okay?

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:01.130
When I lost my voice,

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:06.080
I got scolded for not caring for myself, and lacking self-awareness as a pro.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.910
I'm going to get him back.

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:11.480
"Don't worry about the concert."

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:13.300
"Get some rest."

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:15.960
You're a good guy, Gaku.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:17.120
Well, yeah.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:18.580
Say what?

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:22.330
Boys, have you heard from Tenn?

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:24.520
No.

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:25.340
What happened?

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:26.890
Well, actually...

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:30.590
Nagi and Tamaki aren't here?!

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:32.760
The show starts in an hour.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:36.100
They said they'd arrive by noon.

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:41.470
Manager, you should be overseeing 
them now more than ever.

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:42.630
Sorry.

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:46.020
Knock it off. It's not just her fault.

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:49.770
So cute.

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:50.280
Huh?

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:55.010
In any case, try to be more 
careful in the future.

00:07:55.590 --> 00:07:56.830
Okay.

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:03.000
The way you express affection is going 
to get you into big trouble someday.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:06.710
By the way, I don't see Yamato-san, either.

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:07.930
Huh?

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:09.670
Aw, come on!

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:11.670
What the heck is our leader doing?!

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:16.180
Run faster!

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:17.590
Run!

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:21.430
Tamaki and I have been ready since 
this morning so we wouldn't be late!

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:23.790
I can't believe some of our fans

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:28.440
turned out to be police officers 
who got us involved in a bombing!

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:32.330
Do you think they'll believe we're 
late because we stopped an explosion

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:34.200
at the Tokyo SOLAIRO Tower?

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:36.700
I wouldn't.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:38.700
Of course not.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:44.550
It doesn't look like traffic's moving.

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:46.870
Here is fine.

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:48.710
But sir, you don't look well.

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:50.130
I'm getting off.

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.590
Let me out, please.

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:01.650
Whew. Safe.

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:02.810
Huh?

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:04.990
Huh? Isn't he...

00:09:04.990 --> 00:09:06.530
TRIGGER's...

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:08.560
...Kujo Tenn?

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:13.250
They're not answering their phones.

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:16.620
They could be out of battery 
or dropped them somewhere.

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:17.610
Unbelievable.

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:20.440
Are you okay?

00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:26.150
Yeah. Just a little nervous.

00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:28.420
Why are you nervous?

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:29.670
Are you a TRIGGER fan?

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:30.730
No.

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:35.330
Come to think of it, you 
kinda sing like Kujo Tenn.

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:36.580
I don't—

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:41.230
Riku-kun, you shouldn't 
push yourself too hard.

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:42.390
I'm fine.

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:49.350
I... I... have to watch the man 
who abandoned his family perform.

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:51.940
Abandoned his family?

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:57.050
Are you okay?

00:09:57.050 --> 00:09:59.280
Yes. Thank you.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:02.370
Hey, aren't you gonna be in today's concert?

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:04.950
We were on our way to see it.

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:08.960
So it hasn't gotten out, huh?

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:14.350
I'm really sorry to have 
inconvenienced our fans.

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:15.890
I'm fine—

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:18.970
Doesn't look like you are.

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:19.890
Thanks.

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:21.460
We're not fans.

00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:23.180
We're idols, too.

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:24.180
Idols?

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:28.640
We came to see today's concert 
because... uh, what was it?

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:32.210
Oh, that's it. For simple stimulation.

00:10:32.210 --> 00:10:33.320
Don't be rude.

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:36.570
Really?

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:39.270
Hey, you.

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:39.990
Me?

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:42.210
I'll do anything.

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:44.830
Carry me to the stadium.

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:45.600
Huh?

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:46.240
What?

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:49.000
You're going to perform in your condition?

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.150
No! You can't do that.

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:54.490
I'm asking him.

00:10:54.490 --> 00:10:55.170
Well?

00:10:55.890 --> 00:10:58.170
You're willing to pay anything?

00:10:58.820 --> 00:10:59.420
Yeah.

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:02.430
This taxi will cost you ten King Puddings.

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:03.600
Sure.

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:05.510
Heck yes.

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:08.270
You sure don't ask for much, do you?

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:10.900
Okay, get on.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:12.190
Thanks.

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:13.940
Up we go.

00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:17.280
Hey, you.

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:19.780
Don't talk to me.

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:21.800
I'll lose consciousness 
in about five seconds.

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:23.690
Wake me when we get there.

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:24.320
Now go.

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:25.030
Okay.

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:27.240
He's kind of...

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:29.890
...different from how he acts on TV.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:34.390
I have a twin brother.

00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:35.720
A twin?

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:37.670
We're fraternal, so we don't look alike.

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:40.470
But he's kind and talented.

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:42.680
He was my star.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:46.990
But in middle school,

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:53.350
the little club my parents ran was taken 
by someone in the entertainment industry.

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:54.190
Notice of Closure

00:11:56.810 --> 00:12:00.360
On top of that, he said he wanted my brother.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:04.360
He said my brother was 
the talent of the century.

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:10.120
I waited for my brother to say it'd be okay.

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:11.730
But...

00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:14.210
I'll go with you.

00:12:15.030 --> 00:12:18.000
Let me study under you.

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:26.640
My brother is Kujo Tenn.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:33.600
TRIGGER's center, Kujo Tenn.

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:35.850
My twin brother.

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:44.580
I want to stand where Tenn-nii stood, 
and know what Tenn-nii chose back then.

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:48.880
Have you heard anything?

00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:50.480
Yes. Yes.

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:52.850
You still don't know where Tenn is?!

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:54.330
I'm very sorry.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:55.220
Not yet...

00:12:55.220 --> 00:12:57.200
Hurry up and find him!

00:12:57.200 --> 00:13:00.690
What are you going to do if we find 
TRIGGER's Tenn lying in the street?

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:01.420
Got it!

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:04.400
I wish they'd shut up.

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:06.470
Gaku, you're not worried?

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:07.890
Worried?

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:09.030
Are you stupid?

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:11.470
There's only one place he'd try to go.

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:14.390
I suppose you're right.

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:19.940
Hey.

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:23.030
Can I have twenty King Puddings?

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:25.070
This is pretty hard.

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:25.860
Sure.

00:13:28.180 --> 00:13:30.370
I told you not to talk to me.

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.560
Are you sure you're okay?

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:34.910
I know you don't want to 
miss the concert, but...

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:36.630
I'm a professional.

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:39.890
I provide the same quality 
at every performance.

00:13:40.490 --> 00:13:44.010
I'd never do anything unseemly 
like make my fans worry.

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:48.010
Oh. Is it uncool to make people worry?

00:13:48.630 --> 00:13:52.160
Let's suppose you order 
omelet rice at a restaurant.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:54.350
I want spaghetti with meat sauce.

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:56.770
I want Hamburg steak!

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:59.240
Shut up. You order omelet rice.

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:02.440
Even though you're paying the same price,

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:05.330
how would you feel if it tasted 
good yesterday but bad today?

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:06.530
Disappointed.

00:14:06.930 --> 00:14:08.170
Right?

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:09.870
Concerts work the same way.

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:12.180
If you think it's okay to make them worry,

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:14.850
you're taking advantage of your fans' love.

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:18.420
It's something shameless 
amateurs who lack resolve do.

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:23.440
Here is fine.

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:24.550
Stop the meter.

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:27.550
That'll be 21 King Puddings.

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:29.020
You increased the fare.

00:14:29.020 --> 00:14:29.970
Plus one.

00:14:30.630 --> 00:14:33.490
Thanks. I was able to get some rest.

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:34.420
Sure thing.

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:40.680
We're busy.

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:44.980
But our fans could be busier.

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:47.240
Our job is hard.

00:14:47.890 --> 00:14:52.570
But our fans' lives could be even harder.

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:55.150
We have things we want to do.

00:14:55.150 --> 00:14:59.250
But our fans might have things 
they want to do even more.

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:03.250
Merchandise Sales
 <b>End of Line</b>

00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:07.260
Those people have made time to come 
see us, seeking dreamlike entertainment.

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:11.260
So if we can't make every 
moment the best possible,

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:13.390
there's no point in us standing onstage.

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:17.530
That's how I feel, anyway.

00:15:17.530 --> 00:15:20.040
I promise I'll eat breakfast.

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:22.950
I'll focus when I'm onstage, too.

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:29.400
I don't know what you're talking about, 
but standing onstage gives you energy.

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:33.990
When you receive all that power coming 
from the stands, you can't stand still.

00:15:34.420 --> 00:15:38.040
As fellow idols, I'm sure you understand.

00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:41.060
You're watching the concert tonight, right?

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:43.120
Enjoy your "simple stimulation."

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:44.150
We will.

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:48.380
We'll enjoy your ultimate entertainment.

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:49.890
Later.

00:15:49.890 --> 00:15:50.870
Good luck.

00:15:50.870 --> 00:15:51.860
Take care.

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:53.300
Fight!

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:56.770
Bye-bye.

00:16:03.050 --> 00:16:03.730
Manager!

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:07.030
Sorry we're late.

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:08.200
What have you been doing?

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:13.110
Protecting the peace, carrying a man,
 and earning 21 King Puddings.

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:15.500
Are you making fun of me?

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:17.240
But I worked really hard!

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:19.620
A lot happened.

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:21.720
We ran into TRIGGER's Kujo Tenn.

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:23.370
Kujo Tenn?

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:26.380
Tenn-nii?

00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:28.150
We can talk later.

00:16:28.150 --> 00:16:29.480
The show's about to start.

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:30.300
Let's hurry.

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:31.620
Okay.

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:32.840
All right.

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:40.520
Sorry. Please get on standby.

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:42.600
Gaku, we should get ready.

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:53.300
Tenn.

00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:54.900
You're late, brat.

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:57.570
Really? I'm pretty sure I'm right on time.

00:16:59.060 --> 00:17:00.830
Let's go.

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:02.550
TRIGGER!

00:17:09.610 --> 00:17:10.590
It's starting.

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:18.720
Wow... Ah

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:25.730
Wow

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:28.350
Like the blink of an eye Magic

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:32.150
I had a feeling Ready

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:36.390
The moment we passed each other

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:40.700
I'd fall in love It's a secret night

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:43.450
To an indifferent expression I say No thanks

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:47.410
So I want to make you smile

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:51.800
It's like I'm playing the fool High-tension

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:55.390
Little by little I'll get closer to you

00:17:55.390 --> 00:17:57.380
I'm glad to meet you

00:17:58.070 --> 00:18:01.980
Tell me who the "true" you is

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:02.200
Kujo Tenn is amazing.

00:18:01.980 --> 00:18:07.990
If your hidden heart is Your lies

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:04.930
He could barely stand a moment ago.

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:05.600
Huh?

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:09.270
Looks like he got energy from his fans.

00:18:07.990 --> 00:18:12.400
I'll steal it from above

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:10.680
Tenn-nii...

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:16.240
Let's go Wake me up! (Can't wake up)

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:19.950
Let's dream together (Anywhere)

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:23.740
Twilight for the two of us (Swaying)

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:25.640
I just fall in you

00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:27.410
I just fall in you

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:31.170
Swirling red Lightning

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:35.050
I'll give you sweet memories

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:38.680
Do what you feel Feel so free

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:42.550
We'll become one

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:46.180
Matching rhythms we'll dance together

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:50.020
Leading me astray with those eyes

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:53.730
We'll climb higher and higher Acid love

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:57.260
Tonight I'm going for you

00:18:57.260 --> 00:19:00.120
Trigger

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:07.870
That was really fun.

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:10.370
Yes. It was exciting.

00:19:10.690 --> 00:19:13.880
That Ryunosuke guy was good at dancing.

00:19:14.270 --> 00:19:16.540
He had a great body.

00:19:16.540 --> 00:19:19.170
It was so wild and sexy.

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:21.020
It was awesome!

00:19:21.020 --> 00:19:22.140
The sexiness?

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:24.640
His manly body.

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:28.410
I think you're cuter when you're small—

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:29.310
Shut up! Don't say it!

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:32.830
I couldn't look away.

00:19:32.830 --> 00:19:34.560
Yeah...

00:19:35.030 --> 00:19:37.820
Your brother is amazing.

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:43.200
Yeah. I just... I really...

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:46.450
Riku-kun?

00:19:50.490 --> 00:19:53.240
I want to sing, too.

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:06.120
I want to take powerful steps and 
hear my voice ring out forever

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:08.220
and have a smile that 
makes everyone happy.

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:10.920
I want to get better at singing.

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:14.090
I want to sing, too.

00:20:14.090 --> 00:20:15.730
We haven't in a while.

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:18.260
Yeah. I wanna dance.

00:20:18.260 --> 00:20:21.570
Manager, we can sing and dance now, right?

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:23.860
Yes. The ban's been lifted.

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:26.030
Yes!

00:20:26.470 --> 00:20:29.700
Hey, wasn't that TRIGGER dance cool?

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:31.730
This move?

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:33.790
Nah, it was like this.

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:36.250
Don't dance in the street.

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:38.220
Let's take it from the top.

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:39.520
Come on, Iori.

00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:40.270
You, too.

00:20:40.270 --> 00:20:42.920
Who, me?

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:44.180
Here?

00:20:44.180 --> 00:20:45.860
Come on.

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:48.680
You're hopeless.

00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:01.070
Hey, look at that.

00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:02.940
They're pretty good.

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:29.760
Start running (beyond)

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:36.520
Your imagination... Alive

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:50.420
If you desire something from 
the bottom of your heart

00:21:50.420 --> 00:21:55.200
Risk your life and dive in

00:21:55.510 --> 00:22:00.290
The resolve to discard what's truly important

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:05.420
Is the boat that will take you to new sights

00:22:05.420 --> 00:22:07.970
(Hey man!) Take the strings of your heart

00:22:08.350 --> 00:22:10.510
(Hey man!) And stretch them

00:22:10.510 --> 00:22:13.390
(Say dream!) To the limit

00:22:13.390 --> 00:22:18.310
At the other end you're sure 
to find the Gate to paradise

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:24.260
You'll be the first witness

00:22:24.260 --> 00:22:29.050
Our pounding pulses are Heavenly

00:22:29.050 --> 00:22:34.490
Admit that you can't deny it

00:22:34.490 --> 00:22:38.580
We start... What do your fingertips

00:22:38.580 --> 00:22:42.820
Seek now?

00:22:57.290 --> 00:22:58.350
Someone get some oxygen!

00:22:58.350 --> 00:22:59.460
And ice!

00:23:04.210 --> 00:23:05.440
Gaku.

00:23:05.440 --> 00:23:07.240
You shouldn't push yourself so hard.

00:23:10.520 --> 00:23:13.240
You're actually kind, aren't you?

00:23:13.240 --> 00:23:14.870
Unlike you.

00:23:15.360 --> 00:23:16.790
Are you okay, Tenn?

00:23:17.100 --> 00:23:19.790
Yeah. Thanks, guys.

00:23:20.280 --> 00:23:22.040
For your help during the concert, too.

00:23:22.360 --> 00:23:25.010
We're your group members. 
Of course we helped you.

00:23:25.010 --> 00:23:27.300
You can rely on us for help.

00:23:28.710 --> 00:23:31.090
I love you guys.

00:23:31.670 --> 00:23:33.610
Don't be gross.

00:23:34.440 --> 00:23:35.970
I feel great.

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:38.610
How incredibly stupid!

00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:40.890
What happened?

00:23:41.250 --> 00:23:45.440
Some guys are promoting themselves 
to fans leaving the concert!

00:23:45.440 --> 00:23:46.820
No way.

00:23:46.820 --> 00:23:49.710
But Tenn risked his life to stand onstage.

00:23:49.710 --> 00:23:51.360
Who the hell are they?

00:23:51.360 --> 00:23:55.780
A Takanashi Productions group 
that has yet to debut: IDOLiSH7!

00:23:55.780 --> 00:23:56.990
Huh?
